{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1380287-princess-the-hopeful-bestiary","id":1380287,"title":"Princess: The Hopeful Bestiary","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-10T20:10:56-07:00","id":1380287,"title":"Princess: The Hopeful Bestiary","content":"I don't know what inspired this idea.<br /> The basics of it are what if there were creatures way back in the time of the the Kingdom. And then they went extinct when the Kingdom fell.<br /> Fast forward to the moon landing. The Radiant Queens break free from the dream prison they were trapped in, bringing hope back to the world.<br /> Deep in the Dreamlands the extinct creatures were remembered about &amp; managed to find a door to the physical, waking world that the amanojaku &amp; other Dreamlanders couldn't use for some reason (possibly because these creatures were/are resurrected memories of long extinct creatures, whereas the Dreamlanders are the souls of the citizens of the Kingdom. That's my theory.)<br /> This door they went through had its own rules, giving them bodies of their own.<br /> And, yeah, that's the basics of these collected creatures. Gonna put up some potential examples in my next post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T20:11:53-07:00","id":1380288,"title":"","content":"An iridescent dragon that breaths fire. Any place scorched by it's flames will immediately begin to heal, from the flames &amp; from any harm that had previously been done to it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Savage, uncivilized barbarians.&quot; Despite appearances they are not human, &amp; are somehow permanently divorced of both the Light &amp; the Darkness.<br /> Tough, sturdy combatants.<br /> They have a reputation for not lying, not seeing any real point in it, but this does not mean they can't lie.<br /> Past actions have resulted in them being very untrusting of all the Courts, how this happened is a mystery. This isn't to say that they will never work with any Noble, just that any Noble who tries will have an uphill battle of diplomacy first.<br /> <br /> Light Motes: Tiny, barely sentient/sapient motes of the Light.<br /> <br /> Darkness Motes: Tiny, barely sentient/sapient motes of the Darkness.<br /> <br /> The Order of Crossed Arms: An organization from before the Kingdom fell. The old version was made of ordinary citizens of the Kingdom, but the new version appears to be formed from the coalesced memories of the old version given corporeal form.<br /> They can commonly found helping out at Doctors Without Borders clinics, assisting activists of various ideologies, &amp; providing extra muscle power for any Princesses they find. <br /> Big believers in human rights, they have never &amp; will never follow the beliefs of one Court exclusively.<br /> The greatest weakness of the Order as a whole is that they cannot wrap their heads around the cutthroatedness of modern politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}